"""Improved curator: filters out spam and junk documents.

select(docs, target_sample) -> ordered list of indices into docs (repeats allowed).
Training reads the returned order front to back and stops after exactly T tokens
(T = 9,830,400, see common.py). If the list holds fewer than T tokens it is cycled.
The seed for any randomness is the environment variable CURATE_SEED.

This version prioritizes educational content by filtering out:
1. Documents consisting entirely of stop words in the first 300 characters.
2. Documents appearing to be pure advertisement spam (high ratio of array-like or buy/sell patterns).
3. Documents containing specific high-quality spam phrases without proper context.
"""
